<content><![CDATA[<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>
<multiple-choice question="Which change gives a shallower depth of field (more background blur)?" single-option="" randomize="">
  <input type="checkbox" value="A lower f-stop (a wider aperture)" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="A higher f-stop">
  <input type="checkbox" value="Moving the camera farther from the subject">
  <input type="checkbox" value="Increasing the render resolution">
</multiple-choice>
<true-false-question question="A longer focal length (telephoto) compresses the sense of depth between foreground and background.">
  <input type="checkbox" value="True" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="False">
</true-false-question>
<self-check title="Think it through">
  <p slot="question">How would you use the rule of thirds to frame a product shot?</p>
  <p>Place the product, or its most important feature, on one of the third lines or intersections, leave space in the direction it faces, and keep any horizon on a third line rather than in the middle, unless you want a deliberately symmetrical shot.</p>
</self-check>
